     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Days and dates in Dutch",
     "texto": [
      "Days of the week and months of the year are written in lowercase in Dutch: «maandag» (Monday), «vrijdag» (Friday), «zaterdag» (Saturday), «maart» (March). To indicate the date on which an event takes place, the preposition «op» is placed before it: «op maandag 12 maart» (on Monday 12 March)."
     ],
